<title>FRANCE: ATHLETICS-KIPKETER FACT FILE.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-KIPKETER FACT FILE.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fact file on Wilson Kipketer who set a world indoor 800 metres record of one minute 42.67 seconds on the final day of the world championships on Sunday.</p>
<p>Born December 12, 1970, in Sparta, Kenya. Has lived in Denmark since 1990 but was not allowed to run for his adopted country at the 1996 Atlanta Olympics.</p>
<p>Won world title at 1995 Gothenburg world championships and ranked world number one from 1994 to 96. Broke the previous world 800 indoor record, set by Kenyan Paul Ereng, on the opening day of the championships here.</p>
<p>A student of electronic engineering, his name means &quot;born on the verandah&quot;.</p>
</text>
